  ],
  "description": "Golden bodies of a seat in a running realm (E11, #13250; the feature is #12655): what coax/web/api/seats.c reads and answers on /api/playtest/seats, what it sends the runner that holds a hosted seat's page, and what the runner (coax/web/agent/seat-runner.c) answers and hands the seat's own process. `from` says where a body's bytes came from. api: a running API wrote them in coax/web/api/test.sh (test_room.py with SEAT_CAPTURE), on a throwaway database whose players and keys ended with the run. runner: a running runner wrote them in the same test, for a seat the test made up (its key is the test's seatkey-0001-0123456789). The same test gets each of these again on every run and requires these bytes, but for the values a run decides (ids, times, the player and its key, the API's port). caller: the request the CLI and the realm's page send. source: a refusal or a failure the suite does not reach, as seats.c or seat-runner.c names it. The grant, the list and the act handed to the runner are SQL's (migration 0110 and seats.c), written as jsonb's text: keys by length, then by bytes, with ', ' and ': ' between items. What seats.c and the runner write themselves is compact. seat: an observation, one line as a seat in a running realm printed it (coax/web/realm-seat.coax in headless Chrome, 2026-11-13, against this checkout's page on a local origin and a throwaway API and database; the made realm seat-green has trees, rocks, a house and Maple, a baker, with jump and talk on). The lines were printed by the seat before its writer moved to the codec; the codec reads each and writes the same bytes, and a second run through the codec printed the first three lines byte for byte (the later ones differ by where a walk of a few seconds stopped). An action's values are its members' text, a number as it is typed.",
  "check": "coax/web/tool.sh coax/web/api/seat-wire-goldens.coax proto/verse/realm-seat-v1alpha1.json",
